    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n76613" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παιδο-γόνος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γονή</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>begetting children</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰὼ
				Ζεῦ . . παιδογόνε πόριος Ἰνάχου</span>
			<i>father of a child by</i> the daughter of Inachus, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				629
			</span></i> (lyr.); <i>giving birth to children</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύπρις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					5.53
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Diosc.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φύσις</span> (i. e.
				<i>genitalia</i>) <i><span class="en">
				Ps.-Phoc.
				187
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>giving generative power, making fruitful</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάλης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					4.4
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ὕδωρ</span> a spring <i>with
				aphrodisiac properties</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.18.10
			</span></i>.</div>
